  "name": "Raï algérien (Oran pop-raï)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Oran-region genre that moved from the cheikha and bedoui tradition of gasba flute and guellal drum into the electrified pop-raï of the late 1970s-80s cassette studios under producers like Rachid Baba Ahmed, with Cheb Khaled, Cheb Mami and Chaba Fadela as its stars — synthesizer and trumpet riffs, drum machine or fast 6/8 derbouka over a 4/4 shuffle at roughly 100-130 BPM, and raw first-person Darija lyrics about drink, love and exile delivered in a nasal, melismatic upper-register chest voice.",
